Since the accident occurs one hour after the train starts, it travels with its original speed V for one hour, covering a distance of V miles. After the accident, it continues traveling at 3/4 of its original speed. The time it takes to cover the remaining distance (D - V) at 3/4V is (D - V) / (3/4V). It takes an additional 0.5 hours for the delay, and it arrives 3.5 hours later than planned. We can write the equation:
(T - 1) + (D - V) / (3/4V) + 0.5 = T + 3.5

